; ================================================================
; GINGERBREAD HOUSE — Dual-Material Food Print G-code
; ================================================================
;
; T0 = Cookie dough (walls + roof — all layers)
; T1 = Icing        (decorations on top layer)
;
; Pieces: 4 walls (80x60mm) + 2 roof panels (90x70mm)
; Cookie layers: 3  x  3.0mm = 9.0mm thick
; Total print height: 10.5mm
; Perimeters per layer: 2
; Infill spacing: 5.0mm  (alternating 45°/135°)
; Cookie speed: 800 mm/min  |  Icing speed: 400 mm/min
;
; Piece layout on bed:
;   Wall 1 (front)       origin=(20,20)  size=80x60mm
;   Wall 2 (back)        origin=(115,20)  size=80x60mm
;   Wall 3 (left)        origin=(210,20)  size=80x60mm
;   Wall 4 (right)       origin=(20,95)  size=80x60mm
;   Roof Panel 1         origin=(115,95)  size=90x70mm
;   Roof Panel 2         origin=(220,95)  size=90x70mm
;
; Icing decorations:
;   Wall 1 (front) : outline, arched door, 2 windows
;   Walls 2-4      : outline, 1 window each
;   Roof panels    : outline, ridge line, 2 snowflakes each
;
; Assembly after printing:
;   1. Let pieces cool/set flat
;   2. Join walls at 90° with extra icing
;   3. Attach roof panels at ~45° ridge angle
; ================================================================

; === INITIALIZATION ===
G21              ; millimeters
G90              ; absolute positioning
M82              ; absolute extrusion
G28              ; home all axes
G92 E0           ; zero extruder


; ================================================================
; PHASE 1: COOKIE DOUGH (T0) — all pieces, all layers
; ================================================================

T0  ; switch to cookie dough extruder
G92 E0  ; reset extruder after tool change

; --- Cookie layer 1/3 (Z=3.0mm) ---
